# Two new chairs in Russian: два новых стула
subtitle: "Count chairs and lamps with their adjectives in Russian: оди́н но́вый стул, два но́вых сту́ла, пять но́вых сту́льев, and say what you need with мне нужна́ по́лка."
tags: ["russian","russian numbers","два новых","counting in russian","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/number-cases","grammar/counting-nouns","phrases/shopping"]
thumb: "band \"Two new chairs, one odd ending\" note \"два но́вых сту́ла\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"In order to in Russian: чтобы","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/109-russian-in-order-to.cast"}

