A: Back to my first Saturday, before Masha went home to Moscow: we're in a furniture (@draw shop_w@) shop, a магази́н.
    draw shop

A: My new flat needs chairs. Послу́шайте: no words on the screen yet.
    show masha masha_name tom tom_name

    hide shop_w

    ask "What does the man still need?" listen [{"voice":"a","who":"Tom","text":"Мне нужны́ два сту́ла.","gloss":"I need two chairs."},{"voice":"b","who":"Маша","text":"Вот два но́вых сту́ла. Удо́бные!","gloss":"Here are two new chairs. Comfortable!"},{"voice":"a","who":"Tom","text":"А ещё мне нужна́ по́лка.","gloss":"And I also need a shelf."},{"voice":"b","who":"Маша","text":"Э́та сто́ит пять ты́сяч. Сли́шком до́рого!","gloss":"This one costs five thousand. Too expensive!"}] intro Послу́шайте. options ["a shelf","a lamp","a sofa"] correct 1
        right: По́лка: мне нужна́ по́лка, I need a shelf.
        wrong: Listen for ещё, also: а ещё мне нужна́ …

    ask "What's wrong with the shelf she shows him?" listen same options ["it's too expensive","it's too big","it's not comfortable"] correct 1
        right: Пять ты́сяч: сли́шком до́рого, too expensive.
        wrong: Пять ты́сяч is a price.

    hide masha masha_name tom tom_name shop

A: So how do you count new chairs in Russian? (@draw o_ch2@) The number changes the adjective too, not just the noun.
    draw o_ch1

    erase o_ch1 o_ch2

A: Посмотри́те: the first two lines, written. Мне нужны́ два сту́ла.
    draw n1

B: Вот два но́вых сту́ла.
    draw n2

A: After два, the chair takes the of-ending а: (@draw n_one@) one chair's worth, сту́ла.
    highlight n2 part сту́ла effect underline color #1a8a8a

A: But new says ых: the same ых you met in lesson (@draw n_many@) 106, here as the of-many ending. Но́вых.
    highlight n2 part но́вых effect underline color #1a8a8a

A: So after два, три, четы́ре, the noun counts as one, and the adjective counts as many.
    highlight n_one n_many color #1a8a8a

    erase n1 n2 n_one n_many

A: Посмотри́те: one, two to four, five and more.
    draw tab

A: Оди́н но́вый стул, одна́ но́вая ла́мпа: after one, nothing changes.
    draw tab_r1

B: Два но́вых сту́ла. Две но́вые ла́мпы.
    draw tab_r2

A: With a she-word like ла́мпа, Russians mostly keep the plain plural, но́вые, though (@draw tab_also@) но́вых is right too.
    highlight tab_r2c3 part но́вые effect underline color #5b8c5a

    erase tab_also

B: Пять но́вых сту́льев. Пять но́вых ламп.
    draw tab_r3

A: From five on, both words count as many. And стул has an odd plural, сту́лья, so five chairs are сту́льев.
    highlight tab_r3 part ых$ effect underline color #1a8a8a

    erase tab

A: And the shelf I still need: мне нужна́ по́лка, a shelf is needed to me.
    draw nz2

B: Нужна́ follows the thing you need: мне ну́жен стул, a chair; (@highlight nz2 part нужн[а́]$ effect underline color #b5482e@) мне нужна́ по́лка, a shelf.
    draw nz1

B: Мне нужны́ сту́лья, chairs. And ну́жно you know: (@draw nz3@) мне ну́жно купи́ть, I need to buy.
    draw nz4

A: It changes just like за́нят: nothing, а, о, ы.
    draw nz_like

    erase nz1 nz2 nz3 nz4 nz_like

A: To buy them, six more shop words. Купи́ть, to buy: я куплю́, I'll buy it.
    draw w_buy w_buy_g

A: Покупа́ть is the buying as it happens, or again and again: ты покупа́ешь, you are buying.
    draw w_buy2 w_buy2_g

B: Ка́сса: where you pay. Тако́й, (@draw w_tak w_tak_g@) така́я: such a one, like this.
    draw w_kassa w_kassa_g

B: Сли́шком: too. Пять ты́сяч за по́лку? Сли́шком до́рого!
    draw w_sl w_sl_g w_tag

A: And вы́бери: choose!
    draw w_vyb w_vyb_g

    erase w_buy w_buy_g w_buy2 w_buy2_g w_kassa w_kassa_g w_tak w_tak_g w_sl w_sl_g w_vyb w_vyb_g w_tag

A: Now Masha and I choose a lamp and chairs. (@draw tom_you@) Listen, then tap Practise after the dialogue, and be me.
    show masha masha_name tom tom_name

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    erase talk_1 talk_2 talk_3 talk_4

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    erase talk

    hide masha masha_name tom tom_name tom_you

A: Запо́лните про́пуски: three white chairs, then five.
    draw g1

    ask "Запо́лните про́пуски." gaps g1

B: Три бе́лых сту́ла, пять бе́лых сту́льев.

    erase g1

A: Now build a sentence. In the shop you point at a lamp you like.
    draw b_lamp

    ask "Напиши́те: I need a lamp like this." above b_lamp answer ["мне нужна такая лампа","такая лампа мне нужна","мне нужна вот такая лампа","вот такая лампа мне нужна"] reveal.text "Мне нужна́ така́я ла́мпа." reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833
        keys "АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЪЫЬЭЮЯ "
        right: Мне нужна́ така́я ла́мпа: ла́мпа is a she-word, so нужна́ and така́я both end in а.
        wrong: Ла́мпа is a she-word: нужна́, така́я.

    erase b_lamp question_4_stamp

    draw q1_chairs parallel true

    quiz "Five new chairs: пять ___ сту́льев." reveal.text "Пять но́вых сту́льев." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 280 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        intro: Six questions now, then your score.
        right: Но́вых: from five on, the adjective counts as many too.
        wrong: After пять, both words take the of-many ending.
        * но́вый
        * но́вые
        + но́вых

    erase q1_chairs question_5_stamp

    quiz "I need a shelf: мне ___ по́лка." frame true reveal.text "Мне нужна́ по́лка." reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Нужна́: по́лка is a she-word, so needed ends in а.
        wrong: Needed agrees with the shelf, and по́лка is a she-word.
        * ну́жен
        + нужна́
        * нужны́

    erase question_6_stamp

    draw q3_gap

    ask "Запо́лните про́пуски." gaps q3_gap test t1

B: В магази́не четы́ре удо́бных дива́на.

    erase q3_gap

    ask "What's wrong with the lamp?" voice b options ["it's too expensive","it's too small","it's too heavy"] correct 1 reveal true test t1
        gloss: The lamp is too expensive.
        listen: Ла́мпа сли́шком дорога́я.
        right: Сли́шком дорога́я: too expensive.
        wrong: Listen for сли́шком, too, and the word after it.

    draw q5_ch1 q5_ch2 parallel true

    ask say_it "Мне нужны́ два сту́ла." also ["Два сту́ла мне нужны́."] gloss "I need two chairs." voice a show cue reveal.text "Мне нужны́ два сту́ла." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 300 reveal.style label reveal.size 58 reveal.color #3d3833 test t1

    erase q5_ch1 q5_ch2 question_9_stamp

    ask "Напиши́те: I'll buy five new chairs." frame true answer ["я куплю пять новых стульев","куплю пять новых стульев","пять новых стульев я куплю","я куплю пять стульев новых"] reveal.text "Я куплю́ пять но́вых сту́льев." reveal.style label reveal.size 54 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        keys "АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЪЫЬЭЮЯ "
        right: Я куплю́ пять но́вых сту́льев: after пять, both words count as many.
        wrong: Куплю́, then пять, and after пять both words count as many.

    erase question_10_stamp

    draw eboard

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

A: So the number decides both words: after два, the chair counts as one and new as many.
    highlight e2 color #5b8c5a effect underline

A: From пять, both count as many: пять но́вых сту́льев.
    highlight e3 color #5b8c5a effect underline

    erase eboard

B: Молоде́ц! Два удо́бных сту́ла.
    draw end_masha end_say

    erase end_masha end_say

A: Next time: why we do things. Что́бы, in order to.
    draw next109

